{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":32036,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-sonnet-5","packSha":"63a2b635f2a81f8f6a3a6e64acb0e6dd6e55de515812635866559a458af4a813","packTokens":17116,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":54,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spec","tokens":17036,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":8,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"State, as numbered plain sentences (n = 1, 2, ...), what change this spec asks for. Don't add anything the spec doesn't say. Don't mention IDs.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a user submits an email address and password that match an active account, the portal shall start an authenticated session that carries the user's role and, for a Customer Buyer, the user's customer company.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An active Customer Buyer of company A with password 'Correct#1' when POST /auth/sign-in with that email and 'Correct#1' then Response is 200 with a session; GET /me with that session returns role 'Customer Buyer' and company A, and GET /orders returns 200\",\n    \"Given An active account buyer@a.test when Sign-in is called with buyer@a.test and a wrong password, and separately with unregistered unknown@a.test then Both return 401 with the same message 'Invalid email or password' and no session is issued\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a signed-in user signs out, the portal shall invalidate that user's session.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A signed-in user when POST /auth/sign-out, then a request is made with the same session token then Sign-out returns 200 and the later request returns 401\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If 5 consecutive sign-in attempts for one account fail, then the portal shall lock that account for 15 minutes and reject every sign-in attempt for it during that time with a message saying the account is temporarily locked.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An active account with 4 consecutive failed attempts when A 5th wrong password is submitted, then the correct password 1 minute later then Both responses give the 'account temporarily locked' message and no session is issued\",\n    \"Given An account locked at 10:00 when The correct password is submitted at 10:14 then Sign-in is rejected with the lock message\",\n    \"Given An account locked at 10:00 when The correct password is submitted at 10:15:01 then Sign-in succeeds and the failed-attempt counter is reset to 0\",\n    \"Given An account with 4 consecutive failed attempts when A successful sign-in occurs, followed by 4 more failed attempts and then a sign-in with the correct password then Each of the 4 failed responses is 401 'Invalid email or password' without the lock message, and the final sign-in response is 200 with a session\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a user requests a password reset for their email address, the portal shall email that address a single-use reset link that is valid for 1 hour and lets the user set a new password.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A registered user and an unregistered email address when POST /auth/password-reset is called for each then Both responses are identical; one reset email is sent for the registered user and none for the unregistered address\",\n    \"Given A reset link issued 30 minutes ago when The user sets a new password through it, signs in with old and new passwords, then uses the link again then The new password signs in, the old one returns 401, and the second use of the link is rejected\",\n    \"Given A reset link issued at 09:00 when It is used at 10:00:01, then the user signs in with the old password then The reset response is 400 with an 'expired link' message, and the sign-in response with the old password is 200 with a session\",\n    \"Given An account locked by failed attempts at 10:00 when The user resets the password at 10:05 and signs in with the new password at 10:06 and again at 10:15:01 then The 10:06 sign-in response carries the lock message and no session; the 10:15:01 sign-in response is 200 with a session\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an administrator invites a Customer Buyer for a customer company or an Office Staff user, the portal shall email the invitee a link, valid for 7 days, through which the invitee sets a password and the account becomes active.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An admin invites new@a.test as Customer Buyer of company A when The invitee uses the emailed link 2 days later to set a password, then signs in then The set-password response is 200, the admin user list response shows the account with status Active, and the sign-in response is 200 with a session\",\n    \"Given An invitation sent 7 days and 1 minute ago when The invitee uses the link then The request is rejected as expired and the account stays Invited\",\n    \"Given An expired or pending invitation when The admin resends it then A new link valid for 7 days is emailed and the previous link is rejected\",\n    \"Given An admin when The admin invites a user with role 'Customer Account Manager' then The request is rejected with 400 because the role does not exist\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a user has been deactivated or the user's customer company is inactive, then the portal shall reject that user's sign-in and order submissions while keeping the user's and company's existing orders, invoices and history unchanged.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A deactivated Buyer with 3 past orders when The Buyer signs in with the correct password then Sign-in is rejected with an 'account inactive' message and staff can still open all 3 orders unchanged\",\n    \"Given A Buyer with an open session whose company is then set inactive, and the company has a Received order when The Buyer submits a checkout then Response is 403, no order is created and the existing order stays Received\",\n    \"Given A Buyer with an open session who is then deactivated when The Buyer submits a checkout then Response is 403 and no order is created\",\n    \"Given A deactivated user when An admin reactivates the user and the user signs in with the correct password then The sign-in response is 200 with a session\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an administrator lists users, deactivates or reactivates a user, changes a user's role between Customer Buyer, Office Staff and Administrator, or changes a Customer Buyer's company, the portal shall show each user's role, company and account status, keep every Customer Buyer linked to exactly one customer company, apply the change from the user's next request, and keep the user's historical records.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Users in roles Buyer, Office Staff and Administrator with statuses Invited, Active and Deactivated when An admin lists users then Each user is returned with role, company (Buyers only) and status\",\n    \"Given A signed-in Buyer with past orders when The admin deactivates the user then The user's next request returns 401, sign-in is rejected, and past orders remain visible to staff\",\n    \"Given A Buyer of company A when An admin moves the Buyer to company B and the Buyer lists orders then Only company B's orders are returned\",\n    \"Given An active Office Staff user S when An admin changes S's role to Customer Buyer without a company then Response is 400 and S keeps the Office Staff role\",\n    \"Given An Office Staff user when The user calls PATCH /admin/users/{id} then Response is 403\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall restrict each Customer Buyer to the orders, invoices, prices, delivery addresses and account details of the Buyer's own customer company.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Buyer X of company A, and an order, invoice and invoice PDF of company B when Buyer X requests each by ID then Each returns 404 and no company B data is returned\",\n    \"Given Company A with orders placed by Buyer X, Buyer Y and Office Staff when Buyer X lists orders then All 3 orders are returned and no other company's orders\",\n    \"Given Buyer X of company A when Buyer X requests company B's delivery addresses or account details by ID then Response is 404\",\n    \"Given An unauthenticated client when It calls the catalogue, order or invoice endpoints then All return 401\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall restrict the staff functions listed for Office Staff to Office Staff and Administrators and the administrator functions to Administrators, refusing any other user's request for them without making a change.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A signed-in Customer Buyer when The Buyer calls the staff order queue, an admin price-list endpoint, marks an invoice paid, or requests a sales report then Each call returns 403 and no data changes\",\n    \"Given A signed-in Office Staff user when The user creates a price list, invites a user, or reads the audit history then Each call returns 403 and no data changes\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a Customer Buyer searches the catalogue with a text term, the portal shall return the active products whose name, distributor product code, manufacturer part number or brand contains the term, ignoring letter case.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Active products 'Brake Pad Set' (code BP-1001, MPN 0986494, brand Bosch) and 'Oil Filter' (code OF-200, brand Mann), and retired product 'Brake Disc' when The Buyer searches 'brake', 'bp-10', '6494' and 'BOSCH' then Each search returns 'Brake Pad Set' only; 'Oil Filter' and 'Brake Disc' are never returned\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a Customer Buyer selects a category filter, the portal shall list only active products assigned to that flat, single-level category, combined with any active text or vehicle search.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Active products in categories Filters (2) and Brake system (3) when The Buyer filters by Filters, then Brake system, then clears the filter then The catalogue list responses return 2, then 3, then 5 products\",\n    \"Given Categories Filters (active) and Exhaust (retired) when The Buyer lists categories then Only Filters is returned\",\n    \"Given Category Filters with 'Oil Filter' and 'Air Filter' when The Buyer searches 'oil' with category Filters then Only 'Oil Filter' is returned\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a Customer Buyer searches by vehicle using any combination of make, model, year, engine, fuel type and variant, the portal shall return the active products that have at least one compatibility record matching every supplied value.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given P compatible with Ford Focus 2018 1.0 EcoBoost Petrol Titanium; Q compatible with Ford Focus 2018 1.5 TDCi Diesel when Search make Ford, model Focus, year 2018; then add fuel type Diesel then First search returns P and Q; second returns only Q\",\n    \"Given The same products when Search make Ford, model Focus, year 2005 then Neither P nor Q is returned\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall return for each catalogue product the image, name, distributor product code, manufacturer, unit of sale, pack size, the requesting customer's price and stock status, and on the product detail additionally the description and vehicle compatibility list.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An active product with all fields populated, a price on the customer's list and 2 compatibility records when A Buyer calls the catalogue list and the product detail then The list item has image URL, name, code, manufacturer, unit, pack size, price and stock status; the detail additionally has description and both compatibility records\",\n    \"Given An active product whose last imported quantity is 0 when A Buyer opens its detail then The product is returned with stock status 'Out of stock'\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a Customer Buyer views a catalogue list or product detail, the portal shall show for each product the price excluding tax from the price list assigned to the Buyer's company, in the single configured currency.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Product P priced 10.00 on Standard (company A) and 8.50 on Fleet (company B) when Buyers of A and B request P's detail then A sees 10.00 and B sees 8.50, both marked excluding tax; neither response contains the other list's price\",\n    \"Given The same set-up when An admin reassigns company A to Fleet and A's Buyer requests P's detail again then The product detail response returns price 8.50\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a product has no price on the customer's assigned price list or that price list is deactivated, then the portal shall show the product as 'Price on request' and reject adding it to the basket.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Product Q missing from company A's price list when A Buyer of A views Q and adds Q to the basket then Q shows 'Price on request' and no price; the add returns 422 and the basket is unchanged\",\n    \"Given Company A's assigned price list is deactivated when A Buyer of A views any product then Every product shows 'Price on request'\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall derive each product's stock status from its last imported quantity as Out of stock at 0 or when never imported, Low stock from 1 up to and including the low-stock threshold setting, and In stock above the threshold.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Low-stock threshold 5 when The stock-status method is called for quantities 0, 1, 5 and 6, and for a product never included in a successful import then The method returns Out of stock, Low stock, Low stock, In stock and Out of stock respectively\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the scheduled stock import job reads a valid ERP CSV from the configured file location, the portal shall replace the stored quantity of each product whose distributor product code matches a row, skip rows with unknown codes, and record an import log entry with timestamp, applied and skipped row counts and the skipped codes.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Products BP-100 (qty 3) and OF-200 (qty 0); a valid CSV with BP-100=20, OF-200=4, XX-999=7 in the configured location when The import job runs then BP-100 has 20 (In stock), OF-200 has 4; a Success log entry shows 2 applied, 1 skipped and lists XX-999\",\n    \"Given A completed import when The job finishes then No outbound call or file is sent to the ERP\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If the ERP stock file is missing, unreadable, lacks the product identifier or quantity column, or contains a quantity that is not a whole number of 0 or more, then the import job shall keep all previously imported quantities unchanged and record a failed import with the reason, visible to Office Staff and Administrators.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given BP-100 has qty 20; the new CSV has rows BP-100=-4 or BP-100=abc when The import job runs then BP-100 still has 20 and a Failed log entry names the invalid row\",\n    \"Given No file in the configured location, or a CSV missing the quantity column when The import job runs then All quantities are unchanged and a Failed log entry states the reason\",\n    \"Given A failed import entry when Office Staff and an Administrator read the import log, and a Buyer calls the same endpoint then Staff and admin see the failure with time and reason; the Buyer gets 403\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall keep one saved basket per Customer Buyer across sessions and devices until the Buyer submits it as an order or empties it.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Buyer adds 2 x P (8.50) and 1 x Q (4.00), changes P to 3 and removes Q when The Buyer signs out and signs in on another device then The basket shows 1 line: P x3, line total 25.50, subtotal 25.50\",\n    \"Given Buyers X and Y of the same company when X adds a product to the basket then Y's basket is unchanged\",\n    \"Given A Buyer with a 2-line basket when The Buyer submits the order then The basket is empty afterwards\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a Buyer adds, changes the quantity of, or removes a basket line, the portal shall accept only whole-number quantities of 1 or more and return each line's unit price, line total as unit price times quantity, and the basket subtotal excluding tax.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Product A at 12.50 and product B at 3.00 when The Buyer adds A quantity 4 and B quantity 2 then Line totals are 50.00 and 6.00 and the subtotal is 56.00\",\n    \"Given That basket when The Buyer removes B, then sets A's quantity to 0, -1 and 2.5 then After removal the subtotal is 50.00; each invalid quantity is rejected and A stays at 4\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall calculate the earliest delivery date, in the configured timezone, as the next working day for orders placed before the cutoff time setting and as the second working day for orders placed at or after it, where working days exclude Saturdays, Sundays and admin-listed non-working dates.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Cutoff 14:00, no extra non-working dates when The earliest date is calculated for Monday 13:59, Monday 14:00, Monday 15:00, Friday 15:00 and Saturday 10:00 then Results are Tuesday, Wednesday, Wednesday, the following Tuesday and the following Monday\",\n    \"Given Cutoff 14:00 and that week's Tuesday listed as a non-working date when The earliest date is calculated for Monday 13:00 and for Friday 15:00 of the same week then Results are Wednesday and the following Tuesday\",\n    \"Given Timezone Europe/London and cutoff 14:00 when The earliest date is calculated for 13:30 UTC on a summer Monday (14:30 local) then The result is Wednesday\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a submitted delivery date is not a working day, is before the earliest delivery date, or is more than the booking-horizon setting in days ahead, then the portal shall reject the order submission with a message naming the broken rule.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Order time Monday 15:00, cutoff 14:00, booking horizon 30 days when The Buyer submits with Tuesday, a Saturday, a listed non-working date, and a working day 31 days ahead then Each is rejected with a delivery-date error naming the rule and no order is created\",\n    \"Given The same settings when The Buyer submits with Wednesday then The order is created\",\n    \"Given Earliest date Tuesday and horizon 30 days when The Buyer requests available delivery dates then The list starts at Tuesday and contains only working days up to 30 days ahead\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a Customer Buyer selects a delivery address at checkout, the portal shall offer and accept only the active addresses that Office Staff or Administrators maintain for the Buyer's company.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Company A with 2 active and 1 deactivated delivery address when A Buyer of A requests checkout addresses then Only the 2 active addresses are returned\",\n    \"Given Company A with addresses A1, A2 and company C with address C1 when A Buyer of A submits with C1, and then with A2 then C1 is rejected with 422 and no order is created; A2 is accepted and stored on the order\",\n    \"Given A signed-in Buyer when The Buyer tries to create or edit a delivery address then Response is 403\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If any line's ordered quantity exceeds the product's quantity from the last successful stock import when an order is submitted, then the portal shall reject the submission and return each such line with its available quantity, without subtracting orders placed since the import and without changing stored stock.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given P with imported quantity 5 and an order for 4 x P already placed since the import when A Buyer submits 5 x P then The order is accepted\",\n    \"Given P with imported quantity 5 and Q with imported quantity 0 when A Buyer submits 6 x P, and separately 1 x Q then Both return 422 naming the line with available quantity 5 and 0 respectively; no order is created\",\n    \"Given P with imported quantity 5 when An order for 5 x P is submitted then P's stored quantity remains 5\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a line's price on the customer's current price list differs from the price shown at review, or the product has become 'Price on request', when the order is submitted, then the portal shall reject the submission and return the affected lines with their current prices for review.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given P reviewed at 8.50 and the admin then changes P to 9.00 on the Buyer's list when The Buyer submits with the 8.50 review then Submission is rejected returning P at 9.00; after reviewing again, resubmission creates the order at 9.00\",\n    \"Given A basket line whose product moved to 'Price on request' after it was added when The Buyer submits then Response is 422 naming that line and no order is created\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a checkout that passes stock, price, address and delivery-date validation is submitted, the portal shall create an order with the next sequential number of the form ORD-000123, status Received, the order-time unit prices, delivery address, delivery date and optional note of up to 1000 characters, and empty the Buyer's basket.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Last order number ORD-000122 and a valid basket of 3 x P at 8.50 when The Buyer submits with note 'Rear door' then ORD-000123 exists with status Received, 3 x P at 8.50, total 25.50, address, date and note, a timeline entry Received by the Buyer; the basket is empty; the order appears in the staff queue and its number is returned\",\n    \"Given An order note of 1001 characters when The Buyer submits then Submission is rejected\",\n    \"Given A Buyer in a browser with a 2-line basket when The Buyer goes through checkout then Basket review, address selection, date selection, note and a final review with lines, prices, total, address and date are shown before submit, and a confirmation page shows the order number\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a price list price is changed, the portal shall leave the unit prices of existing orders and invoices unchanged.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Order ORD-000123 with P at 8.50 when The admin changes P to 9.00 and the order is later delivered then The order still shows 8.50 with unchanged total and the invoice line shows 8.50\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When Office Staff change an order's status, the portal shall accept only the next status in the sequence Received, Confirmed, Picking, Out for delivery, Delivered, or a cancellation.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An order in Confirmed when Staff set it to Picking then The change succeeds\",\n    \"Given A Received order and a Confirmed order when Staff set the Received order to Picking, and the Confirmed order to Out for delivery, Delivered or back to Received then Each returns 409 and statuses are unchanged\",\n    \"Given A Picking order when Staff set it to Out for delivery and then to Delivered then Both changes succeed\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an order's status changes, the portal shall add a timeline entry with the new status, the timestamp and the user or system process that made the change.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An order submitted by Buyer X, confirmed by S1 and moved to Picking by S2 when The order timeline is read then It holds Received by X, Confirmed by S1, Picking by S2, each with a timestamp, in time order\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When Office Staff confirm a Received order, the portal shall check every line against the last imported stock quantity and the customer company's active status and, if both pass, set the order to Confirmed and record the confirming user and time; otherwise reject the confirmation naming the reason.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Received order with 3 x P, P imported quantity 10, active company when Staff user S1 confirms it then Status is Confirmed with S1 and time in the timeline, and the Buyer can no longer cancel it\",\n    \"Given A Received order with 8 x P where P's imported quantity is now 5 when Staff confirm it then The request is rejected naming P with available 5 and the order stays Received\",\n    \"Given A Received order whose company was set inactive when Staff confirm it then The request is rejected and the order stays Received\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an order becomes Confirmed, the portal shall email the order recipient a confirmation containing the order number, lines, quantities, unit prices, total, delivery address, delivery date, and every quantity change or line removal made by staff.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An order by Buyer X where staff changed P from 10 to 8 before confirming when Staff confirm it then One email goes to Buyer X with the order number, lines, total, delivery date and address, and 'P: 10 → 8'\",\n    \"Given A staff-created order for company A when Staff confirm it then The confirmation email goes to company A's contact email\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When Office Staff reject or cancel an order that is not Delivered, the portal shall require a reason, set the order to Cancelled, record the reason, acting user and timestamp, and email the order recipient the cancellation with the reason.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Orders in Received and in Out for delivery when Staff cancel each with reason 'Customer phoned' then Both become Cancelled with reason, user and time in the timeline; one email per order with the order number and reason is sent\",\n    \"Given A Received order when Staff reject it without a reason then Response is 400 and status stays Received\",\n    \"Given A Delivered order when Staff cancel it with a reason then Response is 409 and status stays Delivered\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"While an order is in Received status, the portal shall let Office Staff change line quantities, remove lines (keeping at least one line), and change the delivery date, the delivery address to another of the company's addresses, and the note, applying checkout date and address rules and recording each change with user, time, and old and new values in the order's amendment history.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Received order with 5 x P and address A1 when Staff user S changes P to 3 and the address to A2 then The order shows 3 x P with recalculated total and A2; amendment history records S, time, P 5→3 and A1→A2; the Buyer's order detail shows the amendments\",\n    \"Given A Confirmed order when Staff change a line quantity then Response is 409 and the order is unchanged\",\n    \"Given A Received order when Staff set the delivery date to a Saturday, set another company's address, or remove the last remaining line then Each change is rejected and the order is unchanged\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When Office Staff change a line quantity or remove a line on a Received order, the portal shall email the order recipient the order number and each changed line with its old and new quantity.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Received order ORD-000123 by Buyer X with P qty 10 and Q qty 2 when Staff set P to 8 and remove Q then One email to Buyer X contains ORD-000123, 'P: 10 → 8' and 'Q: 2 → removed'\",\n    \"Given A Received order when Staff change only the note then No amendment email is sent\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an order's status changes to Out for delivery, the portal shall email the order recipient a message with the order number stating that the order is out for delivery.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Order ORD-000123 in Picking placed by Buyer X when Staff set it to Out for delivery then One email to Buyer X contains ORD-000123 and 'out for delivery'\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When Office Staff submit an order on behalf of an active customer company, the portal shall apply the same price, stock, address and delivery-date rules as customer checkout and record the staff user as the order's creator.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Company A on Fleet with P at 8.50 when Staff user S creates an order for A with 2 x P, address A1 and a valid date then The order is Received at 8.50, marked created by S, and appears in every A Buyer's order list\",\n    \"Given Company A when Staff submit an order for A using company C's address, a quantity above imported stock, or a date before the earliest delivery date then Response is 422 and no order is created\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When Office Staff open the order queue, the portal shall list all orders with order number, customer, order date, requested delivery date, total and status, filterable by customer, order date range and status.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Orders: A/Received/1 Oct, A/Confirmed/2 Oct, C/Received/2 Oct when Staff filter by customer A, then status Received, then order date 2 Oct–2 Oct then Each result contains 2 orders with all listed fields\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When Office Staff export the delivery list for a date, the portal shall return a CSV with one row per non-cancelled order due that date (any status other than Cancelled, including Received) containing order number, customer, delivery address, contact name, contact phone, delivery date, line summary, note and status.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given For 5 March: one Confirmed, one Received and one Cancelled order; one Confirmed order for 6 March when Staff export the delivery list for 5 March then The text/csv response has a header row and exactly 2 data rows (Confirmed and Received orders) with all listed columns\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When Office Staff or Administrators open the dashboard, the portal shall show the counts of Received, Confirmed, Picking and Out for delivery orders, orders due for delivery today, Unpaid and Overdue invoices, and the result and time of the latest stock import.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given 2 Received, 1 Confirmed, 1 Picking, 1 Out for delivery order, 1 order due today, 3 unpaid invoices of which 1 overdue, latest import Failed when Staff request the dashboard then The response shows those counts and the Failed import with its timestamp\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a Customer Buyer lists orders, the portal shall return every order of the Buyer's company, newest first, with order number, order date, delivery date, delivery address, total and status, filterable by status and order date range.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Company A with orders dated 1, 2 and 3 March from two Buyers and staff, the 2 March one Cancelled when A Buyer of A lists orders then All 3 are returned in order 3, 2, 1 March with all listed fields\",\n    \"Given The same orders when The Buyer filters by status Cancelled, and then by order date 3 March then Each filter returns only the matching order\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a Customer Buyer opens an order of their company, the portal shall return its number, order date, customer, delivery address, requested delivery date, current status, status timeline, lines with quantity, unit price and line total, order total, note and any staff amendments.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Confirmed order with 2 lines, a note and a staff quantity amendment 5→3 when A Buyer of the company opens it then All listed fields are present, the timeline shows Received and Confirmed with timestamps, and the amendment shows 5 → 3\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a Customer Buyer cancels an order of their company, the portal shall accept the cancellation only while the order is in Received status, recording the Buyer and time in the timeline, and otherwise reject it with a message to contact the distributor office.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Received order of company A when A Buyer of A cancels it then Status becomes Cancelled and the timeline names the Buyer and time\",\n    \"Given A Confirmed order of company A when A Buyer of A cancels it then Response is 409 with a message to contact the distributor office and status stays Confirmed\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a Customer Buyer repeats a previous order of their company, the portal shall add each line whose product is active, priced and not Out of stock to the Buyer's basket at the current price-list price and original quantity, adding to the quantity of any existing basket line for that product, and return the other lines flagged as unavailable, without creating an order.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Past order with 2 x P (then 8.00, now 8.50), 1 x R (retired), 1 x Q (Out of stock) when The Buyer repeats the order then The basket gains 2 x P at 8.50; R and Q are flagged and not added; the company's order count is unchanged\",\n    \"Given A basket already holding 1 x P when The Buyer repeats the same order then The basket holds 3 x P\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a Customer Buyer saves the basket as a named template, the portal shall store the template privately for that Buyer and, when the template is added to the basket, use current price-list prices and flag unavailable products.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Buyer B1 saves a basket as 'Weekly Workshop Order' when B1 and B2 (same company) list templates then B1 sees the template; B2 sees none and requesting it by ID returns 404\",\n    \"Given B1's template with 2 x P (now 8.50) and 1 x R (retired) when B1 adds the template to the basket, then deletes the template then The basket gains 2 x P at 8.50, R is flagged; the template no longer appears in B1's list\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an order's status becomes Delivered, the portal shall create one Unpaid invoice with the next sequential number of the form INV-000123, invoice date, customer, billing address, order number, lines with quantity and order-time unit price, net total, tax at the configured rate, and gross total.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An Out for delivery order with 3 x P at 8.50 (net 25.50), tax rate 20%, last invoice INV-000040 when Staff set it to Delivered then Exactly one invoice INV-000041 exists with status Unpaid, net 25.50, tax 5.10, total 30.60 and the order's lines and number\",\n    \"Given An order in Picking when Invoices for its company are listed then No invoice exists for that order\",\n    \"Given Invoice INV-000041 when An admin changes the tax rate to 15% then INV-000041 still shows tax 5.10 and total 30.60\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall report an invoice as Paid when a payment is recorded, as Overdue when unpaid and more than the overdue-days setting has passed since its invoice date, and otherwise as Unpaid.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Overdue days 30 and an unpaid invoice dated 1 March when The status is calculated for 31 March and 1 April then Results are Unpaid and Overdue\",\n    \"Given An invoice dated 1 January with a recorded payment when The status is calculated for 1 April then Result is Paid\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a user lists invoices, the portal shall return to a Customer Buyer every invoice of the Buyer's company, and to Office Staff and Administrators every invoice, each with invoice number, order number, invoice date, gross total and payment status.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Company A has 2 invoices from orders by different Buyers; company C has 1 when A Buyer of A lists invoices; staff list invoices then The Buyer sees A's 2 invoices; staff see all 3, each with the listed fields\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a Customer Buyer of the invoiced company or an Office Staff user downloads an invoice, the portal shall return a PDF containing invoice number, customer, billing address, order number, invoice date, lines with quantity, unit price and line total, net total, tax, gross total and payment status.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Invoice INV-000041 of company A when A Buyer of A and an Office Staff user download the PDF then Both receive application/pdf whose text contains all listed values\",\n    \"Given Invoice of company A when A Buyer of company C requests its PDF then Response is 404\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When Office Staff mark an invoice as paid with a payment date, the portal shall set its status to Paid and record the payment date and the recording user.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An Unpaid or Overdue invoice when Staff user S marks it paid with payment date 2026-10-10 then Status is Paid with payment date 2026-10-10 recorded by S\",\n    \"Given An Unpaid invoice when Staff mark it paid without a date or with a future date, or a Buyer attempts to mark it paid then Staff calls return 400, the Buyer call returns 403, and the invoice stays Unpaid\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an administrator adds, edits or retires a product, the portal shall store its name, unique distributor product code, manufacturer part number, manufacturer/brand, description, category, unit of sale, pack size and status, keeping retired products out of the catalogue but visible on existing orders and invoices.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Product BP-1001 exists when An admin creates another product with code BP-1001, then one with a unique code then The duplicate returns 409; the unique product is created and appears in catalogue search\",\n    \"Given Product P on a Delivered order and its invoice when An admin retires P then P is absent from catalogue list and search, and the order and invoice still show P's line\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an administrator creates, renames or retires a single-level category or assigns a product to one category, the portal shall apply the change to catalogue 